From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windows.ui.xaml: shapes (Rectangle, Ellipse, Line), system text styles, compiled theme dictionaries

NanaZip's status bar separates its fields with Rectangles and styles its text on CaptionTextBlockStyle; there were no shapes and no system text styles. Rectangle (Fill, Stroke, StrokeThickness, RadiusX/RadiusY), Ellipse and Line (X1..Y2) are drawn with Direct2D; a rectangle or ellipse fills the space it is given, a line's size is its far end; caps, joins, dashes, the miter limit and Stretch are kept. The system resources gain the text styles programs base theirs on (Base, Caption, Body, BodyStrong, Subtitle, Title, TitleLarge, Display, Subheader, Header TextBlock styles), by the type ramp of the public design documentation, in the desktop's font. Compiled XAML: Application.Resources, FrameworkElement.Resources and ResourceDictionary.MergedDictionaries/ThemeDictionaries are recognised when the compiler names their owner, and a keyed collection item (node 0x0A) goes into the dictionary under its key (theme dictionaries' "Default", "Light", "Dark"). Interface identity per windows-rs 0.30.0 (MIT); the implementation is ours. Behind the XAML switch of 6131.
---
